PROBE [command]
  The decision services' test drive: its own command line (probe>),
  or one command given after PROBE. Commands:
    model tag tag:level ...   RAT's decision, as deep as the model
                   goes (food.fruit.apple), with its plan: a line a
                   level - the stage (N, R, LD), the contenders and
                   their weights, kept (deadband) or rnd/n
    TRY / RUN model tag ...   a dry run / a real run, this once
    PORTS          the services running (ports, slots)
    SHOW model [tag ...]   every line of the model, or those tags'
                   N R L D weights
    LIKE / DISLIKE model tag [n]   a like up / down n
    SET model [cat\]tag\..\x   a weight set to x, as a sensor would
    SAVE model     its weights saved
    ASK port message   any port asked (ASK DUNGEON Q action? ...)
    PLAN ON|OFF    the plan shown;  DRY ON|OFF  nothing learnt (ON as
                   it starts: probing doesn't change the models)
    HELP, QUIT
